# Calls and remarks to no one, richer (Docs/Design/62-talk.md, phase 7): stall cries by trade with the goods named,
# by season, hour and the day; the Watch's calls; children's games and rhymes; beggars, preachers, carters, sailors;
# the tavern at night and the old on a bench; Ridgemere's quarters and the towns' trades; and moods by trait. Each has
# a cooldown, so a habit shows without wearing thin.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Stall cries, by trade

rule x7_bk_baker_market
when concept=bark self.job=baker here.place=market
cooldown 4h
say Bread! Bread for the hungry, cake for the greedy! | Barley loaves! Rye loaves! Loaves for every belly! | Buns, a penny! Two for a penny if you look sad enough!

rule x7_bk_baker_winter
when concept=bark self.job=baker here.season=winter self.working=yes
cooldown 6h
say Hot buns! Hot as a hearthstone! | Spice bread! A slice'll keep the winter out! | Straight from the oven, steaming in the cold!

rule x7_bk_baker_festival
when concept=bark self.job=baker here.day=festival here.festival self.working=yes
cooldown 6h
say Festival cakes! Honey and seed! | Sweet buns for #here.festival#! | Cakes for the pups, cakes for the grans, cakes for all!

rule x7_bk_smith_market
when concept=bark self.job=smith here.place=market
cooldown 4h
say Knives sharpened while you wait! | Hinges! Hooks! Hasps! | Your old pot mended good as new, for a penny!

rule x7_bk_smith_cold
when concept=bark self.job=smith here.season=winter here.region=frosthollow|coldwater self.working=yes
cooldown 6h
say Skates! Iron runners for the ice! | Crampons for the high path! Don't slip, buy iron! | Shovel blades, hammered thick for the snow!

rule x7_bk_brewer_festival
when concept=bark self.job=brewer here.day=festival here.festival self.working=yes
cooldown 6h
say Festival ale! Strong enough to dance on! | First cup for luck, second for love! | Drink to #here.festival#! Drink to anything!

rule x7_bk_brewer_summer
when concept=bark self.job=brewer here.season=summer here.time=day self.working=yes
cooldown 6h
say Cold cider from the cellar! | Small beer, cool as a cave! | Thirsty work, summer! Wet your whistle!

rule x7_bk_cook_market
when concept=bark self.job=cook here.place=market|street self.working=yes
cooldown 4h
say Pies! Pork pies, mutton pies, mystery pies! | Hot pasties! Hold 'em by the crust! | Sausage in a roll! Eat it walking!

rule x7_bk_cook_winter
when concept=bark self.job=cook here.season=winter|autumn self.working=yes
cooldown 6h
say Hot broth! A penny warms you to the tail! | Stew! Thick enough to plaster a wall! | Roast chestnuts! Hot in the paw!

rule x7_bk_fisher_market
when concept=bark self.job=fisher here.place=market here.time=dawn|day here.region=ridgemere
cooldown 4h
say Fresh off the boats! Still blinking! | Herring by the dozen! Mackerel by the pair! | Crab! Who's brave enough for crab?

rule x7_bk_fisher_shore_dawn
when concept=bark self.job=fisher here.place=shore here.time=dawn
cooldown 6h
say Boats in! Boats in! | Nets up, lads! Let's see what the night gave us. | Good haul! Good haul, look at that!

rule x7_bk_fisher_lake
when concept=bark self.job=fisher here.region=coldwater self.working=yes
cooldown 6h
say Glasswater trout! Cold water, sweet flesh! | Lake perch! Lake pike! Fresh from the deep! | Smoked trout, keeps a month!

rule x7_bk_fisher_fens
when concept=bark self.job=fisher here.region=mirebridge self.working=yes
cooldown 6h
say Eels! Live eels, jellied eels! | Pike from the Long River! | Fen eels, fat as your arm!

rule x7_bk_farmer_spring
when concept=bark self.job=farmer here.place=market here.season=spring
cooldown 6h
say Spring greens! Nettles, leeks, new peas! | First of the radishes! | Eggs! The hens are laying like they're paid for it!

rule x7_bk_farmer_summer
when concept=bark self.job=farmer here.place=market here.season=summer
cooldown 6h
say Strawberries! Sweet as summer! | Beans, peas, lettuces! | Cherries! Spit the stones, not at me!

rule x7_bk_farmer_autumn
when concept=bark self.job=farmer here.place=market here.season=autumn
cooldown 6h
say Apples, pears, the last of the plums! | Marrows! Marrows the size of pups! | Nuts! Cobnuts and walnuts!

rule x7_bk_farmer_winter
when concept=bark self.job=farmer here.place=market here.season=winter
cooldown 6h
say Turnips, onions, good keeping roots! | Cabbages, hard as stones and twice as good! | Salt pork! Hams! Winter's best!

rule x7_bk_crafter_festival
when concept=bark self.job=crafter here.day=festival here.festival self.working=yes
cooldown 6h
say Ribbons for your ruff! Bells for your tail! | Masks! Be someone else for #here.festival#! | Garlands, a penny! Flower crowns, two!

rule x7_bk_crafter_market
when concept=bark self.job=crafter here.place=market
cooldown 4h
say Baskets that won't leak! Well, not much! | Pots, jugs and cups! Drop one, buy another! | Leather, good leather! Belts, straps, purses!

rule x7_bk_healer_winter
when concept=bark self.job=healer here.season=winter|autumn self.working=yes
cooldown 6h
say Cough syrup! Honey and horehound! | Chest rub for the damp! | Willow bark for aches! Sore joints, sore heads!

rule x7_bk_woodcutter_autumn
when concept=bark self.job=woodcutter here.season=autumn|winter here.place=market|street
cooldown 6h
say Kindling! Get your winter wood before the snow! | Firewood! Oak burns long, ash burns hot! | Logs! Split, dry, stacked if you pay extra!

rule x7_bk_woodcutter_oakhaven
when concept=bark self.job=woodcutter here.region=oakhaven self.working=yes
cooldown 6h
say Mind your heads, she's coming down! | Old tree, that. Older than the town. | Warmwood oak. You'll not find a better grain anywhere.

rule x7_bk_herder_spring
when concept=bark self.job=herder here.season=spring self.working=yes
cooldown 6h
say Lambing! Watch for the little ones! | Come on, mother, come on, you can do it. | Twins! Twins again!

rule x7_bk_herder_downs
when concept=bark self.job=herder here.region=larkfield|southmeadow self.working=yes
cooldown 6h
say Fleeces! Downs wool, warmest in the realm! | Hup! Hup, the lot of you! | Up the hill, you daft beasts! Up!

rule x7_bk_miner_frost
when concept=bark self.job=miner here.region=frosthollow self.working=yes
cooldown 6h
say Ore cart coming through! | Down we go. Lamps lit, prayers said. | Good seam, this. Good seam.

rule x7_bk_orchard
when concept=bark self.job=farmer here.region=southmeadow here.season=autumn self.working=yes
cooldown 6h
say Apples! Southmeadow apples, crisp as frost! | Pickers wanted! A penny a basket! | Cider apples, sour as a debt!

rule x7_bk_merchant_festival
when concept=bark self.role=merchant here.day=festival here.festival self.working=yes
cooldown 6h
say #here.festival# prices! Today only! | Gifts for your sweetheart! Gifts for your mother! Gifts for yourself! | Come and spend, it's festival!

rule x7_bk_merchant_rest
when concept=bark self.role=merchant here.day=rest self.working=yes
cooldown 1d
say Mornings only, Restday! Get it while I'm open! | Restday. Half the town at chapel, the other half asleep. | Shutting at noon. The Bright One insists.

rule x7_bk_merchant_dusk
when concept=bark self.role=merchant here.time=dusk self.working=yes
cooldown 6h
say Last call! Everything cheap before I shut! | Closing up! Bargains for the quick! | Going, going, going home!

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- The Watch

rule x7_bk_watch_midnight
when concept=bark self.role=guard self.on_watch=yes here.time=night
cooldown 6h
say Midnight, and all's well! | Lock your doors! Bank your fires! | All quiet! All quiet, and cold!

rule x7_bk_watch_fog
when concept=bark self.role=guard self.on_watch=yes here.weather=fog
cooldown 6h
say Who goes there? | Speak up, whoever you are. | Keep to the lanterns, everyone. Can't see my own paws.

rule x7_bk_watch_crowd
when concept=bark self.role=guard self.on_watch=yes here.crowd=crowd
cooldown 4h
say Single file past the cart! | Make way! Make way there! | No pushing! I see you pushing!

rule x7_bk_watch_festival_night
when concept=bark self.role=guard self.on_watch=yes here.day=festival here.time=night
cooldown 6h
say Fires out! Home, the lot of you! | Festival's over! Over! | Who's that singing? Home, before I sing you to the cells!

rule x7_bk_watch_rest
when concept=bark self.role=guard self.on_watch=yes here.day=rest
cooldown 1d
say Quiet day. Too quiet. | Restday for everyone but the Watch. | Even the thieves take Restday off. Mostly.

rule x7_bk_watch_winter_night
when concept=bark self.role=guard self.on_watch=yes here.season=winter here.time=night
cooldown 6h
say Cold enough to freeze the bell. | Frost on my whiskers and half the night to go. | Anyone got a brazier? No? Course not.

rule x7_bk_watch_city
when concept=bark self.role=guard here.region=ridgemere here.time=dusk|night self.on_watch=yes
cooldown 6h
say Keep moving. No loitering. | Lamps on the corners! Who's put out the lamp? | I see you in that doorway. Out.

rule x7_bk_watch_crime
when concept=bark self.role=guard self.on_watch=yes world.crime=recent
cooldown 6h
say Seen a stranger with full pockets? Tell the Watch. | Lock up tonight. There's thieves about. | Eyes open, everyone. Eyes open.

rule x7_bk_watch_bandits
when concept=bark self.role=guard world.bandits=near here.place=gate
cooldown 6h
say No carts out after dark. Bandits on the road. | Travel in company, or don't travel! | Armed escort leaves at dawn. Join it or wait.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Children

rule x7_bk_rhyme
when concept=bark self.stage=young here.place=street|market|field
cooldown 3h
say One for the baker, two for the bell, three for the wolf who fell down the well! | Ring around the rowan, one wolf falls down! | Tag! You're it! No take-backs! | Watch and thieves! I'm the Watch! You're under arrest!

rule x7_bk_rhyme2
when concept=bark self.stage=young here.time=day
cooldown 3h
say Hide and seek! One, two, ten! Coming! | Bet you can't catch me! | I'm the Bright One and you all have to bow! | Look, I can howl! Owooo!

rule x7_bk_child_autumn
when concept=bark self.stage=young here.season=autumn
cooldown 6h
say Leaf pile! Jump! | Conkers! Who's got conkers? | I found a big acorn! The biggest!

rule x7_bk_child_summer
when concept=bark self.stage=young here.season=summer
cooldown 6h
say Race you to the pond! | It's too hot to wear boots! | I got stung! It doesn't even hurt! It hurts!

rule x7_bk_child_spring
when concept=bark self.stage=young here.season=spring
cooldown 6h
say Lambs! I saw lambs! | There's a nest! Don't touch it! | Mud! Brilliant mud!

rule x7_bk_child_market
when concept=bark self.stage=young here.day=market
cooldown 6h
say Can I have a sweet? One sweet? | Look at that one's hat! | I want the wooden horse. I want it.

rule x7_bk_child_night
when concept=bark self.stage=young here.time=night
cooldown 1d
say I'm not scared of the dark. I'm not. | #mum#? #mum#, where are you? | Was that a ghost? It was a ghost!

rule x7_bk_child_chapel
when concept=bark self.stage=young here.place=chapel
cooldown 1d
say Is the Bright One really watching? All the time? | How long is it till it's over? | Why is everyone whispering?

rule x7_bk_adolescent_dusk
when concept=bark self.stage=adolescent here.time=dusk|night
cooldown 6h
say Nobody's looking. Let's climb the roof. | Bet you won't knock on the old miser's door and run. | Back before my #dad# notices. Easy.

rule x7_bk_adolescent_festival
when concept=bark self.stage=adolescent here.day=festival
cooldown 6h
say Did you see who's dancing with who? | I'm not dancing. I'm not. Well, maybe once. | Somebody nicked a cider. Wasn't me.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Beggars and preachers

rule x7_bk_beggar_market
when concept=bark self.job=beggar here.day=market
cooldown 4h
say Alms! Alms on market day! | Spare a penny from your change, friend! | A copper for an old soldier! Well, an old something.

rule x7_bk_beggar_rest
when concept=bark self.job=beggar here.day=rest
cooldown 6h
say A penny for Restday, for the Bright One's sake. | A penny given on Restday blesses twice. | The chapel's feeding at dusk. Until then, a penny?

rule x7_bk_beggar_night
when concept=bark self.job=beggar here.time=night|dusk
cooldown 6h
say Spare a corner by your fire? | Cold night coming. A coin for a blanket? | Anything. Anything at all.

rule x7_bk_beggar_festival
when concept=bark self.job=beggar here.day=festival here.festival
cooldown 6h
say Spare a crumb of the feast? | Merry #here.festival#! Merrier with a penny! | Even beggars dance at festival. Pay the piper?

rule x7_bk_homeless_cold
when concept=bark self.homeless=yes here.season=winter
priority 1
cooldown 6h
say Another night like the last and I'll not wake. | Doorways. All the doorways are taken. | Paws gone numb. Don't feel them at all.

rule x7_bk_priest_market
when concept=bark self.job=priest here.day=market here.place=market|street
cooldown 6h
say Honest weights, merchants! The Bright One sees your scales! | Give to the chapel's pot, and the Bright One gives back! | Buy what you need, give what you can!

rule x7_bk_priest_festival
when concept=bark self.job=priest here.day=festival
cooldown 6h
say Give thanks, friends, between the cakes! | The Bright One loves a feast! Within reason! | Remember the hungry, as you eat!

rule x7_bk_priest_dawn
when concept=bark self.job=priest here.time=dawn here.place=chapel|street
cooldown 1d
say Morning prayers! The light returns! | Wake, and be thankful! | Come in, come in, the chapel's warm and the Bright One's listening.

rule x7_bk_priest_dusk
when concept=bark self.job=priest here.time=dusk here.place=chapel|street
cooldown 1d
say Evening prayers. Light a candle against the dark. | The kitchen's open for the hungry! | Rest well, all of you. The night's in good paws.

rule x7_bk_priest_storm
when concept=bark self.job=priest here.weather=storm
cooldown 1d
say Even storms pass. Pray, and wait. | Shelter in the chapel, all who need it! | The Bright One holds the sky. Be calm.

rule x7_bk_priest_death
when concept=bark self.job=priest world.death=recent
cooldown 1d
say Remember the dead, and be kind to the living. | Prayers at dusk for the one we lost. | Every life a lamp. One has gone out. Remember it.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Carters, sailors, the road

rule x7_bk_carter_rain
when concept=bark self.job=carter here.weather=rain|storm self.working=yes
cooldown 6h
say Mud to the axles! | Push! Push, she's stuck! | Every road in the realm's a river today.

rule x7_bk_carter_dawn
when concept=bark self.job=carter here.time=dawn self.working=yes
cooldown 6h
say Wagon leaving! Room for two more! | Load up, load up, we're off at sunrise! | Who's riding? Penny a mile, or walk!

rule x7_bk_carter_winter
when concept=bark self.job=carter here.season=winter
cooldown 6h
say Road's iced from here to the next town. | Chains on the wheels, or we'll be in the ditch. | Nobody travels in this but fools and carters.

rule x7_bk_sailor_dawn
when concept=bark self.job=sailor here.place=shore here.time=dawn
cooldown 6h
say Tide's turning! All aboard who's coming! | Cast off! Cast off! | Red sky this morning. Keep your hoods close.

rule x7_bk_sailor_storm
when concept=bark self.job=sailor here.weather=storm
cooldown 6h
say Make fast! Double the lines! | Nobody's sailing in this. Nobody sane. | The Sound's angry tonight.

rule x7_bk_sailor_tavern
when concept=bark self.job=sailor here.place=tavern
cooldown 6h
say Here's to the ones the Sound kept! | Sing! Sing, you landlubbers! | Seven days at sea, one night ashore. Pour!

rule x7_bk_harbour
when concept=bark self.quarter=harbour_hill|docks|wharf here.region=ridgemere here.place=shore|street
cooldown 6h
say Ship in from the south! Look at her sails! | Load her up! Steady with that crate! | Watch the gangplank, it's slick as an eel!

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Nights, taverns, benches

rule x7_bk_tavern_merry
when concept=bark here.place=tavern here.time=night self.humour=merry self.stage=adult|old
cooldown 6h
say I love you all. Every one. | One more song! One more! | Who moved the door? Somebody's moved the door!

rule x7_bk_tavern_singer
when concept=bark here.place=tavern here.time=dusk|night self.talk=chatty
cooldown 6h
say And then, and then, listen, the cart went in the river! | I'll tell you what's wrong with this town. Everything! | Shh! Shh. Listen. I've a story.

rule x7_bk_tavern_quiet
when concept=bark here.place=tavern self.talk=quiet
cooldown 6h
say Just the one. | Mm. Good ale. | Quiet corner. Perfect.

rule x7_bk_street_late
when concept=bark here.place=street here.time=night self.humour=merry
cooldown 6h
say La la la... which way's home? | This way. No. That way. | Hello, lamp post! Lovely night!

rule x7_bk_bench_clear
when concept=bark self.stage=old here.place=street|market here.weather=clear here.time=day
cooldown 6h
say Sit down, sit down, there's room on the bench. | Watch them all rush. Rush, rush. Where to? | Sun on my face. That'll do me.

rule x7_bk_old_spring
when concept=bark self.stage=old here.season=spring
cooldown 1d
say Another spring. Didn't think I'd see it. | Blossom. Same blossom as when I was a pup. | Spring's for the young. I'll watch.

rule x7_bk_old_winter
when concept=bark self.stage=old here.season=winter
cooldown 1d
say One more winter. One more. | My father died in a winter like this. | Cold gets in the bones and stays.

rule x7_bk_old_festival
when concept=bark self.stage=old here.day=festival
cooldown 1d
say I danced at this festival sixty years ago. Sixty! | Too loud. Lovely, but too loud. | They don't make cakes like they used to.

rule x7_bk_old_chapel
when concept=bark self.stage=old here.place=chapel
cooldown 1d
say I knew the old priest. Better sermons. | I've been sitting in this pew longer than the pew's been here. | Bright One, take me gently, when it's time.

rule x7_bk_old_young
when concept=bark self.stage=old here.crowd=busy|crowd
cooldown 6h
say Young ones everywhere. Where did they all come from? | Walk, don't run! Nobody listens. | When I was young the street was half as full and twice as clean.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Ridgemere's quarters

rule x7_bk_heights
when concept=bark self.quarter=heights here.region=ridgemere self.wealth=rich
cooldown 1d
say Servants! Where are the servants? | Such a view. Shame about the smell from below. | One can't get a decent cheese anywhere any more.

rule x7_bk_works
when concept=bark self.quarter=works here.region=ridgemere
cooldown 1d
say Smoke in my lungs again. | Furnace never sleeps, so neither do we. | Soot on everything. Soot in my supper.

rule x7_bk_office
when concept=bark self.quarter=office here.region=ridgemere
cooldown 1d
say Three copies of everything. Always three. | Stamp, sign, file, stamp. | Permit for this, permit for that. Permit to breathe, next.

rule x7_bk_suburbs
when concept=bark self.quarter=suburbs here.region=ridgemere
cooldown 1d
say Quiet out here. Just how I like it. | Long walk into the city. Worth it. | Hens are laying. Life's good.

rule x7_bk_estate
when concept=bark self.quarter=estate here.region=ridgemere
cooldown 1d
say The master's horses are on the lawn again. | Lawns to cut, hedges to trim, never a thank you. | Big house. Small wages.

rule x7_bk_commons
when concept=bark self.quarter=commons here.region=ridgemere
cooldown 1d
say Good honest street, the Commons. | Everyone knows everyone. That's the trouble. | Mind the gutter, it's full again.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Moods by trait

rule x7_bk_merry_dawn
when concept=bark self.humour=merry here.time=dawn
cooldown 1d
say Morning, world! Morning, sky! | Up and at it! Who's with me? No one? Fine! | Lovely morning to be a wolf.

rule x7_bk_short_crowd
when concept=bark self.temper=short here.crowd=busy|crowd
cooldown 6h
say Move! Some of us have places to be! | Out of the way! | Who walks this slow? Who?

rule x7_bk_nervy_crowd
when concept=bark self.temper=nervy here.crowd=crowd
cooldown 6h
say So many people. Too many people. | Somebody's touching my purse. No? Sorry. | I need air. I need air.

rule x7_bk_devout_dawn
when concept=bark self.piety=devout here.time=dawn
cooldown 1d
say Bright One, thank you for the morning. | Another day given. Use it well. | First light. A blessing every time.

rule x7_bk_restless
when concept=bark self.drive=restless
cooldown 1d
say Same street. Same street, every day. | One day I'll take the road and not look back. | What's over the hills? I'd like to know.

rule x7_bk_content
when concept=bark self.drive=content here.weather=clear here.time=dawn|day
cooldown 1d
say Ah. Can't ask for more than this. | Good day. Good, plain day. | Nothing wrong with the world this morning.

rule x7_bk_dry_market
when concept=bark self.humour=dry here.day=market
cooldown 1d
say Ah, market day. Everything a penny dearer and twice the shouting. | Wonderful. Crowds. My favourite. | If one more wolf treads on my tail, I'm buying a cart.

rule x7_bk_warm
when concept=bark self.warmth=warm here.crowd=busy|crowd
cooldown 1d
say Mind how you go, everyone! | Lovely to see the street full. | #greet#, all! #greet#!

rule x7_bk_cold
when concept=bark self.warmth=cold here.crowd=busy|crowd
cooldown 1d
say Out of my way. | Everyone so loud. | Why must they all talk at once?

rule x7_bk_sly
when concept=bark self.honesty=sly here.place=market|street
cooldown 1d
say Something for nothing, anyone? No? Shame. | I know a wolf who knows a wolf. Ask me. | Fine goods, no questions. No answers either.

rule x7_bk_quiet_hum
when concept=bark self.talk=quiet
cooldown 1d
say Hm hm hm. | Mm. | There. That's done.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- The weather, as it falls on the trades

rule x7_bk_fog_shore
when concept=bark here.place=shore here.weather=fog
cooldown 6h
say Ships'll ground in this. | Ring the fog bell! Somebody ring it! | Can't see the water. Can hear it, though.

rule x7_bk_snow_frost
when concept=bark here.region=frosthollow here.weather=snow
cooldown 6h
say Snow on snow on snow. | Shovels out! Path's gone again. | Pretty, if you don't have to walk in it.

rule x7_bk_autumn_field
when concept=bark self.job=farmer|laborer here.place=field here.season=autumn
cooldown 6h
say Bring it in! Bring it in before the rain! | Sheaves up! Stook them proper! | Last field! Last field and then the harvest supper!

rule x7_bk_spring_field
when concept=bark self.job=farmer here.place=field here.season=spring
cooldown 6h
say Plough's stuck again. | Seed's in. Now pray. | Rooks! Off my seed, you thieves!

rule x7_bk_summer_heat_work
when concept=bark self.working=yes here.season=summer here.weather=clear here.time=day
cooldown 1d
say Water! Who's got the water bucket? | Too hot to work. Working anyway. | My tongue's hanging out like a pup's.

rule x7_bk_festival_soon
when concept=bark world.festival=soon
cooldown 1d
say Festival soon! I'm counting the days. | Got to get my coat brushed before the festival. | Not long now. Not long.

rule x7_bk_wedding_recent
when concept=bark world.wedding=recent
cooldown 1d
say What a wedding that was. | My feet still ache from the dancing. | Did you see the cake? Three tiers!

rule x7_bk_bandits_near
when concept=bark world.bandits=near self.travelling=yes
priority 1
cooldown 6h
say Eyes open. They hit a caravan on this road. | Stick together. Nobody straggles. | Every bush, a bandit. Every shadow.
